1
00:00:01,460 --> 00:00:03,295
SHELDON:
I must say, Leonard...

2
00:00:03,462 --> 00:00:08,634
...when I first heard your idea
for Giant Jenga I was skeptical.

3
00:00:10,636 --> 00:00:14,640
I can't blame you,
Tiny Twister was a complete bust.

4
00:00:14,806 --> 00:00:16,058
Oh. But I was wrong.

5
00:00:16,225 --> 00:00:20,812
The looming threat of being crushed
under a pile of lumber...

6
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:23,357
...does add a certain spice.

7
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:25,651
I've never felt so alive.

8
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:26,985
[CHUCKLES]

9
00:00:27,152 --> 00:00:28,403
[KNOCK ON DOOR]

10
00:00:30,656 --> 00:00:34,159
Oh, hello, Alex. Let me go get you
last night's recordings.

11
00:00:34,368 --> 00:00:35,494
What recordings?

12
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:37,996
Remember when you told me
I talk in my sleep?

13
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:42,334
It occurred to me that like most things I say,
it's probably pure gold.

14
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:45,337
So I started recording it all and...

15
00:00:45,504 --> 00:00:47,172
...now Alex gets to comb through...

16
00:00:47,339 --> 00:00:50,008
...eight hours of what I like to call
"Sheldon After Dark."

17
00:00:51,635 --> 00:00:52,844
-Hey, Leonard.
-Hey.

18
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,805
Just playing a little Giant Jenga.

19
00:00:54,972 --> 00:00:57,599
I know, I'm the one who
had to buy him the helmet.

20
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:00,477
So do you have plans this weekend?

21
00:01:00,644 --> 00:01:04,356
Most of Saturday's gonna be figuring out
where to put this game when we're done.

22
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:06,024
How about you?

23
00:01:06,441 --> 00:01:09,861
I'm gonna go hear Kip Thorne give a
lecture about subatomic space-time.

24
00:01:10,028 --> 00:01:13,991
Oh, that's his take on John Wheeler's
quantum foam. That should be great.

25
00:01:14,199 --> 00:01:15,534
Well, you can come with me.

26
00:01:15,701 --> 00:01:18,537
I'd love to, but I'm supposed to
hang out with Penny.

27
00:01:18,704 --> 00:01:22,040
-Well, bring her.
-Oh, she's not really into in that kind of stuff.

28
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:27,045
Well, if you want to hear about the lecture,
I can tell you all about it at work...

29
00:01:27,212 --> 00:01:29,047
...or, you know, over dinner sometime.

30
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:30,382
What?

31
00:01:34,136 --> 00:01:36,221
Giant Jenga! I win!

32
00:02:02,456 --> 00:02:04,082
Oh, come on, that can't be true.

33
00:02:04,249 --> 00:02:05,417
The Egg Salad Equivalency

34
00:02:05,584 --> 00:02:07,085
I did the research. Tony the Tiger...

35
00:02:07,252 --> 00:02:11,882
...Dig 'Em the frog, Cap'N Crunch, Toucan
Sam, Count Chocula, Trix the Rabbit...

36
00:02:12,090 --> 00:02:13,925
...Snap, Crackle and Pop.

37
00:02:14,676 --> 00:02:17,262
Not one cereal mascot is a girl.

38
00:02:18,805 --> 00:02:21,725
It's a total breakfast sausage fest.

39
00:02:22,768 --> 00:02:24,102
Are we done with this?

40
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:28,982
Almost. Franken Berry, Boo Berry,
Sugar Bear, and the Honey Nut Cheerio Bee.

41
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:31,276
I believe his name is Buzz.

42
00:02:31,443 --> 00:02:34,988
Terrific. Something weird happened
and I don't know what to do about it.

43
00:02:35,197 --> 00:02:37,074
-What's going on?
-Sheldon's assistant...

44
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:38,325
...asked me on a date.

45
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:40,160
How could you do that to me?

46
00:02:40,327 --> 00:02:42,788
You know I've been working it
with Alex for weeks.

47
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:45,457
Working it? You can't even talk to her.

48
00:02:45,624 --> 00:02:48,126
I talk with my eyes.

49
00:02:54,466 --> 00:02:58,136
You look like my little cousin when
he's dropping one in his diaper.

50
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:02,683
She knows I have a girlfriend.
It's so weird.

51
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:04,476
Oh, my God. You're loving this!

52
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:05,811
To my bones.

53
00:03:05,977 --> 00:03:08,021
[CHUCKLING]

54
00:03:08,187 --> 00:03:10,189
I'm not gonna do anything about it.
I love Penny.

55
00:03:10,357 --> 00:03:14,486
It's just nice to have a young, attractive
woman sniffing around the goods.

56
00:03:14,653 --> 00:03:20,992
I both hate you and want to be you.
This is Ryan Gosling all over again.

57
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:25,204
Aww. Gentlemen. What is on the
conversational menu this morning?

58
00:03:25,455 --> 00:03:27,249
Leonard stole my woman,
and he knew...

59
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:30,419
...I was only six to eight months away
from making my move.

60
00:03:31,336 --> 00:03:33,004
I didn't steal anyone.

61
00:03:33,171 --> 00:03:36,049
Your assistant is totally hitting on this jerk
and he loves it.

62
00:03:36,215 --> 00:03:39,803
Well, that's not acceptable. I'm her boss.

63
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:42,556
She needs to be solely focused
on my needs...

64
00:03:42,723 --> 00:03:47,310
...not distracted by your pasty,
androgynous brand of sexuality.

65
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:50,605
I'm androgynous?

66
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:55,068
Oh, please. Look at you with your
pouty bee-stung lips.

67
00:03:55,861 --> 00:03:57,237
What do you think I should do?

68
00:03:57,404 --> 00:04:00,282
I say you tell Alex your heart
belongs to Penny.

69
00:04:00,449 --> 00:04:03,702
I provide her a shoulder to cry on,
then roughly half a year later...

70
00:04:03,869 --> 00:04:05,078
...I give it to her good.

71
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:12,711
I want to thank you all for coming on such
short notice. In the past...

72
00:04:12,878 --> 00:04:15,756
...I've reached out to each of you
individually...

73
00:04:15,922 --> 00:04:21,260
...but I believe my present situation
requires the collective wisdom of the group.

74
00:04:21,428 --> 00:04:26,265
Which, as you can see from
your commemorative t-shirts, I've dubbed...

75
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:30,353
...Sheldon Cooper's Council of Ladies.

76
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:34,274
What is happening?

77
00:04:34,441 --> 00:04:39,279
I need your advice about a delicate
workplace situation.

78
00:04:39,446 --> 00:04:42,949
To protect those involved,
I'll be changing their names.

79
00:04:43,116 --> 00:04:44,451
Who's involved?

80
00:04:44,618 --> 00:04:47,496
A short, bespectacled colleague of mine...

81
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:51,458
...who lives in the shadow
of his brilliant roommate.

82
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:56,379
Uh.... Let's call this colleague
Ricardo Shilly-Shally.

83
00:04:57,464 --> 00:05:00,091
-You're talking about Leonard.
-No, no.

84
00:05:00,258 --> 00:05:06,473
Shilly-Shally has red hair and
briefly served in the Mexican Navy.

85
00:05:09,308 --> 00:05:12,312
Anyway, despite the fact
that he has a girlfriend...

86
00:05:12,479 --> 00:05:14,773
...Shilly-Shally has been the recipient...

87
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:18,485
...of inappropriate workplace flirtations
from a young lady.

88
00:05:18,693 --> 00:05:21,696
-It's your assistant Alex, isn't it?
-No.

89
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:26,535
No, it's Tondelaya della Ventimiglia.

90
00:05:27,661 --> 00:05:29,871
What the hell is going on
with Leonard and Alex?

91
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:33,500
I'm sorry, who's talking about
Leonard and Alex?

92
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,670
Fine. Ricardo and Tondelaya.

93
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:39,673
It's not really about
Ricardo and Tondelaya.

94
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,842
It is really about her boss...

95
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:46,680
...who doesn't quite know how to handle
this situation and could use your advice...

96
00:05:46,930 --> 00:05:50,684
...which is surprising, because
Dr. Einstein Von Brainstorm...

97
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:54,563
...he's usually pretty smart
about these things.

98
00:05:55,522 --> 00:05:56,815
Ugh. I'm gonna kill her!

99
00:05:56,982 --> 00:06:00,068
You've got nothing to worry about.
Leonard would never cheat on you.

100
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:04,406
She's right. But say the word, I got a lab
full of cocaine-addicted monkeys...

101
00:06:04,573 --> 00:06:06,032
...with nothing to lose.

102
00:06:07,659 --> 00:06:10,537
One of them could end up
in the back seat of her car.

103
00:06:10,829 --> 00:06:12,581
Or her shower.

104
00:06:14,332 --> 00:06:17,419
Ladies, ladies, please.
We're not here to talk about Penny.

105
00:06:17,586 --> 00:06:21,380
We're here to talk about me.
I mean Einstein Von Brainstorm! Darn it.

106
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:23,884
All right, I guess the cat's out of the bag.

107
00:06:24,551 --> 00:06:27,429
Let me explain what's going on.
Ricardo is really Leon--

108
00:06:27,596 --> 00:06:29,764
We know what's going on, Sheldon!

109
00:06:31,099 --> 00:06:32,559
But what should I do?

110
00:06:32,976 --> 00:06:35,604
Alex is your employee.
If she's doing something that's...

111
00:06:35,770 --> 00:06:38,397
...making Leonard uncomfortable,
you should talk to her.

112
00:06:38,565 --> 00:06:40,942
Oh, he's not uncomfortable at all.
He's loving it.

113
00:06:41,109 --> 00:06:44,403
He's strutting around
like he's 5-foot-6.

114
00:06:45,404 --> 00:06:46,740
What? He's loving it?

115
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:49,408
Sheldon, you need to talk to Alex
right away.

116
00:06:49,576 --> 00:06:51,578
Talk to her. That's all you've got?

117
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:54,581
With a cool name like
Sheldon Cooper's Council of Ladies...

118
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:56,583
...I really expected more.

119
00:06:56,917 --> 00:06:59,085
Give me back the t-shirts.

120
00:07:10,555 --> 00:07:15,143
Alex, check my schedule.
What does my afternoon look like?

121
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:19,272
I think it's pretty wide open. Oh, wait.
Here's something at 4:00.

122
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,942
"Give Alex a talking to"?

123
00:07:23,777 --> 00:07:25,820
Well, that snuck up on us, didn't it?

124
00:07:26,780 --> 00:07:30,617
-Is there a problem?
-Let's not call it a problem...

125
00:07:30,784 --> 00:07:32,619
...let's call it an opportunity.

126
00:07:32,786 --> 00:07:34,454
To solve a serious problem.

127
00:07:35,330 --> 00:07:36,539
What did I do?

128
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,959
You don't know? Oh, you poor dear.

129
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:42,128
Your ovaries are squirting so much
goofy juice into your brain...

130
00:07:42,295 --> 00:07:44,339
...you don't know which way is up.

131
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:51,513
You made an inappropriate
sexual advance towards Dr. Hofstadter.

132
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:55,350
What? I didn't make a sexual advance
on anybody.

133
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,686
Now, there's no need to get defensive.

134
00:07:57,852 --> 00:08:00,105
I'm not unsympathetic to your plight.

135
00:08:00,313 --> 00:08:04,192
My father used to say
that a woman is like...

136
00:08:04,359 --> 00:08:08,321
...an egg salad sandwich
on a warm Texas day.

137
00:08:10,323 --> 00:08:11,992
What?

138
00:08:12,158 --> 00:08:15,996
Full of eggs and only appealing
for a short time.

139
00:08:17,205 --> 00:08:19,332
This conversation
is making me uncomfortable.

140
00:08:19,498 --> 00:08:21,376
Yeah, you and me both, sister.

141
00:08:23,837 --> 00:08:28,842
Please understand, I don't hold you
responsible for your behavior.

142
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:34,014
From an evolutionary standpoint,
you're a slave to your desire to reproduce.

143
00:08:34,180 --> 00:08:35,724
But during the work day...

144
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:40,020
...when you feel possessed
by amorous intent, may I suggest...

145
00:08:40,186 --> 00:08:43,648
...you suppress it by leafing through
this illustrated book...

146
00:08:43,815 --> 00:08:45,734
...of sexually transmitted diseases.

147
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:48,153
[SHELDON SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

148
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:50,405
Oh, yes. Check out this oozy doozy.

149
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:54,743
I have to go.

150
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:58,413
So does this fellow, but he
can't without it burning like hot soup.

151
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,252
[LEONARD WHISTLING]

152
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:07,213
Hey, pretty lady.

153
00:09:08,214 --> 00:09:09,924
You seem extra happy.

154
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:12,635
-I guess I am.
-Any particular reason why?

155
00:09:12,844 --> 00:09:14,721
No, just having a good day.

156
00:09:14,888 --> 00:09:17,390
This morning Sheldon fell asleep
on the way to work...

157
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:19,893
...so I got to listen to the radio.
That was crazy.

158
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:22,062
Mm-hm. Anything else?

159
00:09:22,228 --> 00:09:26,232
Mm.... I found this quiz online called
"Which Star Trek Character Are You?"

160
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:28,777
It only took me four tries
to get Captain Kirk. Heh.

161
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:30,779
-That's great.
-Oh.

162
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:32,530
[MIMICS CAPTAIN KIRK]
It. Was.

163
00:09:32,697 --> 00:09:33,907
[GIGGLES]

164
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:36,910
Hmm.
I'm glad you're having such a great day.

165
00:09:37,077 --> 00:09:41,873
And the one thing that could make it
better is an evening with my special girl.

166
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,083
Oh, and who's that?

167
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:44,751
What do you mean?

168
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:47,420
I just didn't know if you meant me
or Alex.

169
00:09:48,046 --> 00:09:49,464
Why would I mean Alex?

170
00:09:49,672 --> 00:09:52,300
Because I know she hit on you
and I know you liked it!

171
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:55,720
[NERVOUSLY]
What?

172
00:09:56,387 --> 00:10:00,266
Don't play dumb with me,
Ricardo Shilly-Shally!

173
00:10:05,730 --> 00:10:08,274
I'm missing something.

174
00:10:09,943 --> 00:10:12,278
Did you say something to Penny
about Alex?

175
00:10:12,445 --> 00:10:18,493
Yes, and a fat lot of good it did me.
All she did was get mad at you.

176
00:10:20,078 --> 00:10:21,788
Why would you do that?

177
00:10:21,955 --> 00:10:23,665
I needed advice about a woman.

178
00:10:23,832 --> 00:10:27,418
I would have asked you, but
if the last few years have proven anything...

179
00:10:27,585 --> 00:10:30,130
...it's that you can't tell a uterus
from a unicycle.

180
00:10:31,631 --> 00:10:35,510
At least I know not to blab to a girl
about somebody flirting with her boyfriend.

181
00:10:35,677 --> 00:10:36,719
[CELL PHONE RINGING]

182
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:38,972
Good to know.
A few more helpful hints like that...

183
00:10:39,139 --> 00:10:41,641
...you may find yourself
on the Council of Ladies.

184
00:10:41,808 --> 00:10:43,810
Hello?

185
00:10:44,853 --> 00:10:47,814
I see. What time?

186
00:10:48,606 --> 00:10:49,983
Very well, then.

187
00:10:50,525 --> 00:10:54,988
Huh. That was the Human Resources
Department at the university.

188
00:10:55,155 --> 00:10:59,200
Apparently my assistant, Alex,
has filed a complaint accusing me of...

189
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,828
...inappropriate behavior
in the workplace.

190
00:11:01,995 --> 00:11:04,497
Oh, my God. What did you do?

191
00:11:04,998 --> 00:11:08,168
Oh. Let me think....

192
00:11:08,334 --> 00:11:09,836
Nothing, I'm a delight.

193
00:11:15,967 --> 00:11:17,719
Human Resources Department.

194
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:20,305
Human Resources Department.

195
00:11:20,513 --> 00:11:22,223
Human Resources Department.

196
00:11:23,099 --> 00:11:24,184
Come in?

197
00:11:26,102 --> 00:11:29,022
-Hello.
-Ah. Dr. Cooper, have a seat.

198
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:30,315
Thank you.

199
00:11:30,481 --> 00:11:32,650
I called you in today because
your assistant...

200
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:35,486
...Alex Jensen has
lodged a complaint against you.

201
00:11:35,653 --> 00:11:39,657
So I've been told. But I can't understand
what she has to complain about.

202
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:42,952
She has a front row seat as I
make scientific history...

203
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:46,998
...there's string cheese in my mini-fridge
and that's for anyone...

204
00:11:48,625 --> 00:11:52,837
...and just yesterday I led her away
from a life of sexual promiscuity...

205
00:11:53,004 --> 00:11:56,549
...by making her look at pictures
of disease-ridden genitalia.

206
00:12:02,680 --> 00:12:06,309
Cancel my next appointment.
This is gonna take a while.

207
00:12:07,518 --> 00:12:10,104
Dr. Cooper, you said things
to your employee...

208
00:12:10,271 --> 00:12:12,357
...that you just cannot say
in the workplace.

209
00:12:12,982 --> 00:12:14,025
Like what?

210
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:16,319
Well, according to Ms. Jensen you said...

211
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:19,864
...that she was a
"slave to her biological urges"...

212
00:12:20,031 --> 00:12:23,493
...and called her an "egg salad sandwich."

213
00:12:26,454 --> 00:12:28,289
I don't even know what that means...

214
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:31,251
...but I'm gonna go ahead
and tell you you can't say it.

215
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:35,546
Oh, I see the confusion here.

216
00:12:35,713 --> 00:12:38,925
Alex thought I was singling her out. No.

217
00:12:39,092 --> 00:12:43,846
I meant that all women
are slaves to their biological urges.

218
00:12:44,055 --> 00:12:45,390
Even you.

219
00:12:47,558 --> 00:12:49,227
You're a slave.

220
00:12:53,398 --> 00:12:55,191
I'm a what?

221
00:12:56,234 --> 00:13:00,071
I'm just saying. At a certain point
in a woman's menstrual cycle--

222
00:13:00,238 --> 00:13:01,990
Uh-uh. Oh.

223
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:04,075
You can't talk about that either.

224
00:13:04,284 --> 00:13:07,370
Your language is entirely inappropriate,
and I'm going to advise...

225
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:09,330
...that you shut your mouth right now.

226
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:12,375
I don't see why I'm the one being
persecuted here.

227
00:13:12,542 --> 00:13:15,878
Dr. Hofstadter was bragging about his
sexual desirability...

228
00:13:16,045 --> 00:13:17,630
...to anyone who would listen.

229
00:13:18,715 --> 00:13:22,260
Howard Wolowitz spent two years
using university resources...

230
00:13:22,427 --> 00:13:24,595
...building a six-breasted sex robot.

231
00:13:25,305 --> 00:13:29,309
And at the office Christmas party,
I heard Rajesh Koothrappali...

232
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:32,312
...refer to you several times
as "Brown Sugar."

233
00:13:35,398 --> 00:13:40,278
Hofstadter, Wolowitz and
that last one was Rajesh Koothrappali?

234
00:13:40,445 --> 00:13:45,742
Yes. But in his defense,
